# What `docker build` must NOT ship into the build context. Every
# apps/*/Dockerfile opens its pruner stage with `COPY . .`; the builder stage
# then runs its own `bun install --frozen-lockfile` against the pruned lockfile,
# so nothing below is ever used from the context.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, because the Dockerfiles read them from the context:
#   - `.env.example` / `.env.<BUILD_ENV>`  → COPY .env.${BUILD_ENV} .env
#   - `apps/*/nginx.conf`                  → copied into the nginx runner stage
#   - `package.json`, `turbo.json`, `bun.lock`, `bunfig.toml` → `turbo prune`

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output — every stage rebuilds from source.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
storybook-static
**/storybook-static
.next
**/.next

# Tooling caches.
.turbo
**/.turbo
.cache
**/.cache
.bun-cache
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test artefacts.
.vitest
**/.vitest
test-results
**/test-results
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
blob-report
**/blob-report
coverage
**/coverage
**/junit.xml

# History. `turbo prune` walks the filesystem, not git.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
